### Describe the bug

generateTestHeaderString throws a plain error when given an async-only CryptoProvider (like SubtleCryptoProvider), with no mention of generateTestHeaderStringAsync.

constructEvent already handles this — it catches the error and tells us to use constructEventAsync instead (from #1828). generateTestHeaderString never got the same fix, even though generateTestHeaderStringAsync has existed since #2048.

This is probably what caused #1942 — someone hit this same bare error and didn't know an async version existed.

### To Reproduce

1. Create a SubtleCryptoProvider
2. Call webhooks.generateTestHeaderString({ payload, secret, cryptoProvider })
3. Error message has no mention of generateTestHeaderStringAsync

If I call constructEvent the same way with the same provider, that error DOES mention constructEventAsync.

### Expected behavior

generateTestHeaderString should give the same kind of hint constructEvent does, but pointing to generateTestHeaderStringAsync.

### Code snippets

```JavaScript
const provider = new SubtleCryptoProvider();

try {
  stripe.webhooks.generateTestHeaderString({
    payload: '{}',
    secret: 'test_secret',
    cryptoProvider: provider,
  });
} catch (e) {
  console.log(e.message);
  // "SubtleCryptoProvider cannot be used in a synchronous context."
  // no mention of generateTestHeaderStringAsync
}
```

